<ContentLayout
  title="Watch Multiple Twitch Streams at Once | Stream Mix"
  description="Watch multiple Twitch streams and chats at once. Learn how to add channels, arrange the grid, and troubleshoot Twitch embeds in Stream Mix."
  heading="Watch multiple Twitch streams at once"
  platform="twitch"
>
  <p>
    Stream Mix puts several Twitch channels and chats in one draggable browser
    workspace, with each panel showing video, chat, or both.
  </p>

  <h2>How to add multiple Twitch streams</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Paste a channel URL such as <code>https://www.twitch.tv/twitch</code> into
      the Stream Mix header.
    </li>
    <li>
      Twitch is selected automatically. Choose Stream + Chat, Stream, or Chat.
    </li>
    <li>Select <strong>Add</strong> and repeat for the remaining channels.</li>
    <li>Drag and resize the resulting windows to arrange your layout.</li>
  </ol>

  <p>
    You can also select Twitch manually and enter only the channel name. Channel
    URLs and names are supported; clips and video-on-demand URLs are not.
  </p>

  <h2>Twitch embed behavior</h2>
  <p>
    Stream Mix uses Twitch’s official player and chat embeds—it does not
    restream broadcasts. Twitch requires the containing domain, so Stream Mix
    supplies <code>streammix.app</code> in production and <code>localhost</code>
    {" "}during local development.
  </p>

  <p>
    Chat and account actions can depend on Twitch authentication, cookies, and
    browser privacy settings. See Twitch’s{" "}
    <a href="https://dev.twitch.tv/docs/embed/" rel="external"
      >official embed requirements</a
    > for the platform-level rules.
  </p>

  <h2>Twitch troubleshooting</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>URL rejected:</strong> use the main channel URL or the channel name,
      not a clip, category, search, or VOD page.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Channel appears offline:</strong> the window remains valid and can
      stay in your saved layout for the next broadcast.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Chat or account controls fail:</strong> check the channel directly
      on Twitch, then test without strict tracking protection or content blockers.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Several streams stutter:</strong> lower secondary stream quality, mute
      unused audio, use Chat-only panels, or minimize some streams.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Related guides</h2>
  <p>
    See the <a href="/guides/watch-multiple-streams">setup guide</a>, or add{
      " "
    }
    <a href="/guides/watch-multiple-youtube-streams">YouTube</a> and{" "}
    <a href="/guides/watch-multiple-kick-streams">Kick</a> streams to the same workspace.
    The <a href="/faq">FAQ</a> covers broader playback and privacy questions.
  </p>

  <p>
    <a href="/" class="btn btn-primary">Open the Twitch multistream viewer</a>
  </p>
</ContentLayout>
